{"text": "CEDAR HOLLOW CARE & REHABILITATION CENTER -- QUARTERLY CARE PLAN NOTE\nResident: WHITEHORSE-DUBOIS, Eleanor (\"Nell\")        Room 214-B\nMRN CH-0038817   DOB 01/26/1929 (97 y/o)   Admit 09/14/2023\nMedicare no. 1EG4-TE5-MK73    Medicaid ID MT00447318\nAttending: Olumide Fashola, MD (NPI 1654581465)     IDT date: 6/11/2026\nPresent: K. Vandersloot RN (MDS coord.), Faith Morningstar (social services),\ndietary, activities; daughter/POA Renata Dubois-Kim by phone (406-555-0121).\n\nDIAGNOSES: vascular dementia (BIMS 6, down from 8); CHF, EF 35%;\nstage 2 pressure injury, sacrum (noted 5/29/2026, 1.5 x 1 cm, improving);\nhx of falls -- last fall 4/2/2026, no injury. Pacemaker in place\n(model/serial on wallet card: PJN 7204419), last interrogation OK.\n\nMEDS (filled by Bitterroot Long-Term Care Pharmacy): furosemide 40 mg daily (Rx\n#6621047), metoprolol succinate 25 mg, donepezil 10 mg at bedtime, Tylenol PRN.\nQuetiapine was discontinued 5/1/2026 per gradual dose reduction; no increase in\nbehaviors per night staff.\n\nCODE STATUS / PREFERENCES: DNR, POLST on chart signed 10/02/2023. Resident is\none of Jehovah's Witnesses -- NO blood products; card in chart, Renata confirms.\nElders from her congregation visit Thursdays; resident enjoys this.\nSpeaks Salish with visitors and responds better to her nickname than to\n\"Mrs. Dubois\" -- staff reminded.\n\nNUTRITION: weight 104 lb, down 4 lb in 90 days. Mechanical soft diet,\nfortified shakes twice daily. Braden score 14.\n\nGOALS NEXT 90 DAYS\n1. Sacral wound closed by next review; turn q2h, air mattress in place.\n2. No falls with injury; bed alarm, non-skid socks, toileting schedule.\n3. Weight stable within 2 lb.\n\nFAMILY / FINANCIAL: Ms. Dubois-Kim asked about the private-pay balance\n($3,912.40 for March, before Medicaid approval) and whether the personal\nneeds allowance ($50/mo) can go to the beauty shop account. Social\nservices to follow up with the business office. Next review 9/10/2026.\nShe is the last surviving charter resident of the facility; activities\nwould like to mark her 100th when the time comes.\n\nSigned: Kristy Vandersloot, RN   06/11/2026 15:40", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "315 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Eleanor Dubois", " Renata Dubois-Kim", "Kristy Vandersloot"], "companies": ["CEDAR HOLLOW CARE & REHABILITATION CENTER", "Bitterroot Long-Term Care Pharmacy", "Jehovah's Witnesses"]}, "topics": {"places": ["CEDAR HOLLOW CARE & REHABILITATION CENTER"], "health": ["vascular dementia", "CHF", "stage 2 pressure injury", "falls", "pacemaker", "furosemide", "metoprolol succinate", "donepezil", "Tylenol", "Quetiapine", "weight 104 lb", "Braden score 14", "weight stable"], "sensitive": [], "names": ["Eleanor", "Nell", "Renata", "K"]}, "chunks": 1, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.19999999925494194, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 27687.89999999851, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 41, "text": "CEDAR HOLLOW CARE & REHABILITATION CENTER", "kind": "company", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "CEDAR HOLLOW CARE & REHABILITATION CENTER"}, {"start": 80, "end": 106, "text": "WHITEHORSE-DUBOIS, Eleanor", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Eleanor Whitehorse-Dubois"}, {"start": 109, "end": 113, "text": "Nell", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Nell"}, {"start": 138, "end": 148, "text": "CH-0038817", "kind": "record", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "CH-0038817"}, {"start": 155, "end": 165, "text": "01/26/1929", "kind": "dob", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "01/26/1929"}, {"start": 183, "end": 193, "text": "09/14/2023", "kind": "date", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "09/1